sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant A as Admin User
    participant AGW as Admin API Gateway
    participant ACTRL as Admin Controller
    participant ASVC as Admin Service
    participant REPO as Repository Layer
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Tables
    participant C as Redis Cache Cluster
    participant BUS as RabbitMQ Event Bus
    participant LOG as Centralized Logger
    participant JOB as Background Sync Job (GitHub Releases)

    Note over A,LOG: Example — Admin updates FAQ, modifies ticket status, or reviews logs

    A->>AGW: Authenticated HTTP Request (PUT /admin/faq/:id or PATCH /admin/ticket/:id)
    AGW->>ACTRL: Forward Request to Admin Controller
    ACTRL->>ASVC: Validate Role & Input
    ASVC->>REPO: Perform DB Operation (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)
    REPO->>DB: Execute SQL Query
    DB-->>REPO: Operation Successful
    REPO-->>ASVC: DB Confirmation

    alt FAQ or Docs Update
        ASVC->>C: Invalidate / Refresh Cached Entry
        C-->>ASVC: Cache Updated
    else Ticket Update
        ASVC->>BUS: Publish "TicketUpdated" Event (async)
        BUS-->>ASVC: Event Queued
    else Logs View
        ASVC->>REPO: Query Logs from DB
        DB-->>REPO: Return Log Data
        REPO-->>ASVC: Logs Ready
    end

    ASVC->>LOG: Log Admin Action (Audit Trail)
    LOG-->>ASVC: Logged OK
    ASVC-->>ACTRL: Operation Success / Data Ready
    ACTRL-->>AGW: HTTP 200 Response
    AGW-->>A: Display Confirmation / Data

    Note over JOB,DB: Background Job periodically fetches GitHub Release Notes via API and stores metadata (auto-sync)
